            <ArticleTitle>Chronic chest pain in children and adolescents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>685-6, 691-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chest pain is a common symptom of older children and adolescents. The majority of the conditions causing it are benign and self-limiting. Almost all diagnoses can be made with a thorough history and physical examination. Most important, the patient and parents need to be assured that there is no heart defect and that there is no imminent danger of dying.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
